      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Run the existing Dynamo LRU graph-order workaround from RegionAC.apply.\n- Add a regression test covering checkpoint replay after a static-to-dynamic compile transition.\n\n## Why\n\nRegionAC overrides the base activation-checkpointing apply method, so it skipped the process-wide setup already used by the other checkpointing policies. With pipeline parallelism, one rank can execute a compiled function with several input shapes before an earlier checkpoint is replayed. Dynamo LRU ordering can then choose the newer dynamic graph during recomputation even though the original forward used the static graph, causing a checkpoint tensor-metadata mismatch.\n\nThis uses the existing workaround for pytorch/pytorch#166926 and does not change checkpoint policy or model numerics.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- python -m pytest -q tests/unit_tests/gpu/test_activation_checkpoint.py tests/unit_tests/gpu/test_remat.py\n- 27 passed, 55 subtests passed\n- Focused pre-commit hooks passed; Pyrefly was skipped locally because this worktree does not have the configured PyTorch source search path.",
